    "description": {
      "type": "String",
      "label": "Description",
      "value": "<p>Ponies are smaller horses &ndash; those 14 hands or shorter &ndash; their breeds often originating from areas with harsher habitats, such as Kislev or World's Edge Mountains. They are strong for their size and notoriously mischievous, usually deployed for driving, riding, or as pack animals. They are also used to teach youths how to ride horses, or offered at travelling carnivals for children's pony rides. They come in a variety of sizes, but most are around 13 hands at the withers.</p>"
